erface migration first (new params/ports and submodule propagation), then align cycle-by-cycle buffer staging against the Python model; mismatch in staged capture order causes early deterministic assertion failures.\nFor detect-sequence extension tasks, first eliminate X-propagation on boolean control checks by using explicit 4-state-safe comparisons (`=== 1'b1`) in detect/FSM guards.\nAfter X issues are removed, the dominant failures are usually cycle-alignment mismatches against the harness Python model (buffer capture and conjugate-select timing), not arithmetic correctness.\nIn this harness, fixing `o_proc_detected` unknowns exposed that `proc_buffer_i_dff` update timing still lags expected model behavior, so next work should focus on exact per-cycle staging parity in detect path registers.\nKeep `timescale 1ns/1ns` in staged RTL while iterating cocotb/Icarus to avoid timing instability masking logic bugs."
